    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point atop the order, as **Yordan Alvarez** (87.42) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.12) represent our elite offensive pillars. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a high-ceiling matchup against V\u00e1squez, whose 4.97 xERA provides a soft landing for his elite .471 xwOBA. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is a priority start, not only for his 82.12 efficiency score but for his critical role in mitigating our team-wide need for stolen bases. With wind blowing out and a favorable matchup against Dobnak, he is perfectly positioned to provide a multi-category contribution. We are also capitalizing on the shaky form of Bieber, forcing both **Trea Turner** (77.93) and **Kyle Schwarber** (77.21) into the lineup; their aggressive order placements and positive SP skill adjustments make them high-leverage plays in our 5x5 hunt.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Josh Smith**, who sits at 33.53\u2014well below our 40.0 floor. Despite his utility versatility, he was hamstrung by a brutal matchup against Luzardo (3.20 xERA) and a drop in the lineup order to the #8 hole. The combination of an elite arm and limited situational upside made him an easy bench candidate compared to the balanced production expected from **Colt Keith** (53.46) or **Junior Caminero** (61.00). We continue to monitor the status of **Caleb Durbin**, whose absence from the confirmed lineup today is a significant loss for our speed metrics; he remains the primary bench threat to reclaim a spot as soon as he returns to action. Owners should keep a close eye on the weather and potential late lineup shifts, particularly regarding the status of **Yordan Alvarez**, whose \"Lineup Pending\" designation is the only remaining variance in an otherwise optimized configuration.",
